ame>Laurent</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Fries</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Long-term randomized controlled trials of tailored-print and small-group arthritis self-management interventions</article-title><source>Medical Care</source><year>2004</year><volume>42</volume><fpage>346</fpage><lpage>354</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15076811</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1097/01.mlr.0000118709.74348.65</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B10"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Fu</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Fu</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>McGowan</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Shen</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name><name><surname>Zhu</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Yang</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Mao</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Zhu</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Ding</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name><name><surname>Wei</surname><given-names>Z</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Implementation and quantitative evaluation of chronic disease self-management programme in Shanghai, China: randomized controlled trial</article-title><source>Bulletin of the World Health Organization</source><year>2003</year><volume>81</volume><fpage>174</fpage><lpage>182</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12764513</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B11"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Taylor</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Bury</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Chronic illness, expert patients and care transition</article-title><source>Sociology of Health &#x00026; Illness</source><year>2007</year><volume>29</volume><fpage>27</fpage><lpage>45</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17286704</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B12"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Audrey</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Holliday</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Parry-Langdon</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Campbell</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Meeting the challenges of implementing process evaluation within randomized controlled trials: the example of ASSIST (A Stop Smoking in Schools Trial)</article-title><source>Health Educ Res</source><year>2006</year><volume>21</volume><fpage>366</fpage><lpage>377</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16740670</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1093/her/cyl029</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B13"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Baksi</surname><given-names>AK</given-names></name><name><surname>Al-Mrayat</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Hogan</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Thomas</surname><given-names>Z</given-names></name><name><surname>Whittingstall</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Wilson</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Training programme for peer advisors in diabetes: are they the expert patients in diabetes?</article-title><source>Pract Diabetes Int</source><year>2005</year><volume>22</volume><fpage>119</fpage><lpage>124</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1002/pdi.779</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B14"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Barlow</surname><given-names>JH</given-names></name><name><surname>Bancroft</surname><given-names>GV</given-names></name><name><surname>Turner</surname><given-names>AP</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Volunteer, lay tutors' experience of the Chronic Disease Self-Management Course: being valued and adding value</article-title><source>Health Educ Res</source><year>2005</year><volume>20</volume><fpage>128</fpage><lpage>136</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15314037</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1093/her/cyg112</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B15"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Backett-Milburn</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Wilson</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Understanding peer education: insights from a process evaluation</article-title><source>Health Educ Res</source><year>2000</year><volume>15</volume><fpage>85</fpage><lpage>96</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10788205</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1093/her/15.1.85</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B16"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Brown</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Hennings</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Caress</surname><given-names>AL</given-names></name><name><surname>Partridge</surname><given-names>MR</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Lay educators in asthma self management: Reflections on their training and experiences</article-title><source>Patient Education and Counseling</source><year>2007</year><volume>68</volume><fpage>131</fpage><lpage>138</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17662568</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/j.pec.2007.05.009</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B17"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Larkey</surname><given-names>LK</given-names></name><name><surname>Alatorre</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Buller</surname><given-names>DB</given-names></name><name><surname>Morrill</surname><given-names>C</given-names></